menu "Virtual Wi-Fi (QEMU)"

    config ESP_WIFI_QEMU
        bool "Enable virtual Wi-Fi driver for QEMU"
        default y
        help
            Replaces the real Wi-Fi blob driver with a lightweight MMIO shim
            that bridges to the host wpa_supplicant daemon via Unix ctrl socket.
            Enable this option only when targeting the Espressif QEMU fork.
            Must NOT be enabled for real hardware builds.
            Default is y: this component is ONLY added to EXTRA_COMPONENT_DIRS
            when building for QEMU, so defaulting to y means no sdkconfig
            change is needed in stock samples.

    config ESP_WIFI_QEMU_AP_FAKE_CLIENTS
        int "Fake AP clients to inject on softAP start"
        depends on ESP_WIFI_QEMU
        range 0 4
        default 2
        help
            When the firmware starts in AP or APSTA mode, the QEMU shim
            posts this many synthetic WIFI_EVENT_AP_STACONNECTED events
            with deterministic MACs (02:QE:00:00:00:NN) and AID = NN+1.
            Stock softAP samples then log the join messages and
            esp_wifi_ap_get_sta_list returns these entries.  Set to 0 to
            keep the AP empty (legacy behaviour).

endmenu
